WEBVTT

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.943
The more senior you get, the more relaxed you have to be.

00:00:05.073 --> 00:00:08.241
People think that's because you delegate more,

00:00:08.335 --> 00:00:10.415
or because you've seen it all.

00:00:10.514 --> 00:00:11.294
No.

00:00:11.409 --> 00:00:15.141
The real reason: it's the only way to survive.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.942
The higher you go, the more decisions land on you.

00:00:18.962 --> 00:00:23.448
Harder ones. Less information. More at stake.

00:00:23.529 --> 00:00:26.622
A stressed brain makes bad calls.

00:00:26.642 --> 00:00:29.598
That's physiology. Not attitude.

00:00:29.618 --> 00:00:35.183
Under stress, the part of your brain that weighs options goes silent,

00:00:35.292 --> 00:00:38.362
and the part that reacts takes over.

00:00:38.494 --> 00:00:41.498
You stop weighing. You start reacting.

00:00:41.628 --> 00:00:43.412
So when the pressure goes up,

00:00:43.572 --> 00:00:46.720
that's exactly the moment to slow down.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:50.316
Calm isn't the reward for being senior.

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:52.718
Calm is a must.
